    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmin.ai\n\n### Description\n\nThis is in the *MiniAi-textobject-builtin* section of the vim documentation .  There is that table with the examples of text objects, and of where your selection will be if your select them.  Under `i` for the first line, it says `[4;10]` but I think it should be `[3;11]`. \n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.1                                                                                                                    NVIM v0.10.1                                                                                                                            Build type: RelWithDebInfo                                                                                                              LuaJIT 2.1.1725453128                                                                                                                   Run \":verbose version\" for more info    \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nrun :h mini.ai go to the builtin text objects part of the documentation, put the cursor on an asterisk on the first line. Enter `vi[`, for example, in normal mode. \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPositions 4-10 should be selectet\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nPositions 3-11 are selected",
